+### November 23, 2026
+
+- We announced the deprecation of the Claude Opus 4.5 model (`claude-opus-4-5-20251101` and `claude-opus-4-5`), with retirement on the Claude API scheduled for January 22, 2027. We recommend migrating to Claude Opus 5.5. See Migrating from Claude Opus 4.5 or earlier. To check which dates apply on other platforms, see Model deprecations.
+- We've launched Enterprise Frontier Safeguards (EFS) in beta on Claude Platform, Claude Platform on AWS, and Claude Models on Google Cloud (Anthropic managed). EFS is Zero Data Retention (ZDR) for eligible organizations that use Claude's most capable models. Anthropic doesn't retain your prompts and responses. Encrypted copies of them, called Sealed Safety Data, go to a bucket in your own cloud account. A workspace on Anthropic-managed storage isn't on EFS, because Anthropic stores that workspace's Sealed Safety Data. To get access, see Setup guide.
+- We've added two event types to organization webhooks, which are in beta. We send `external_storage.failed` when a bucket that you use as customer-owned storage fails our daily check, and `external_storage.recovered` when it passes again.
